["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"ess","stream_identity":"01a0cabe-67c1-7103-8e43-bb0ee2ca8073","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"MIG72ec4a235fdc30ff6c529befd120683695e397df0c6d5b3e9b5ce9dff17b8133","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/interpreted-eventual-views","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":3,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"# Story: an eventual view is really eventual under the interpreter\n\n## Outcome\n\nA view's rows are derived from what the model declares — `source`, `filter`, `params`, `order_by`\nand `shape` — and a view declared `consistency: eventual` lags behind the writes that feed it rather\nthan answering immediately.\n\nA single in-memory map is tempted into immediacy by its own architecture, which makes this the first\nthing an interpreter gets wrong. `reference.rs` lags by `Billing::DEFAULT_LAG` further reads and\nsays why: a suite that never waits never tests the word `eventual`, and the first real projection\nwould find that out in production.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nEvery view scenario in `examples/billing`'s committed suite reports the same result under `--target\ninterpreted` as under `--target billing`, including those that read an eventual view before and\nafter the lag.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe interpreter's view path and its lag model. No change to `reference.rs` or to the suite.\n","owner":"ess","relations":[{"decomposes":"epic:model-driven-interpretation"},{"serves":"vision:O2"},{"depends_on":"story:interpreted-command-execution"}],"scope":[{"confidence":"cited","path":"crates/specify/ess-compiler/src/ir.rs"},{"confidence":"inferred","path":"crates/specify/ess-domain/src/view.rs"},{"confidence":"inferred","path":"crates/specify/ess-primitives/src/predicate.rs"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"crates/verify/ess-conformance"},{"confidence":"inferred","path":"crates/verify/ess-conformance/src/interpret.rs"},{"confidence":"inferred","path":"crates/verify/ess-conformance/src/lib.rs"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"crates/verify/ess-conformance/src/reference.rs"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"crates/verify/ess-conformance/src/target.rs"}],"status":"draft","summary":"Views derive rows from source, filter, params, order_by and shape, and eventual consistency lags","tags":["priority-high"],"title":"An eventual view is really eventual under the interpreter"},"lifecycle_state":"draft"}},"id":"MIG72ec4a235fdc30ff6c529befd120683695e397df0c6d5b3e9b5ce9dff17b8133","lifecycle_state":"recorded","revision":3,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["aep.entity","MIG72ec4a235fdc30ff6c529befd120683695e397df0c6d5b3e9b5ce9dff17b8133"]}]